    <exercise number="255" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>2. If $$f = g \circ h,$$ when reversing the chain rule, $$\frac{d}{dx}(g \circ h)(x) = g^{\prime}\left. ({h(x)} \right)h^{\prime}(x),$$ should you take $$u = g(x)$$ or $$u = h(x)?$$</paragraph>
