    <exercise number="313" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Show that the average value of $$f(x)$$ over an interval $$\left\lbrack {a,b} \right\rbrack$$ is the same as the average value of $$f\left( {cx} \right)$$ over the interval $$\left\lbrack {\frac{a}{c},\frac{b}{c}} \right\rbrack$$ for $$c &gt; 0.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Setting $$u=cxu=cx$$ and $$du=cdxdu=cdx$$ gets you $$1bc-ac\int a/cb/cf(cx)dx=cb-a\int u=au=bf(u)duc=1b-a\int abf(u)du.1bc-ac\int a/cb/cf(cx)dx=cb-a\int u=au=bf(u)duc=1b-a\int abf(u)du.$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="314" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the area under the graph of $$f(t) = \frac{t}{\left( {1 + t^{2}} \right)^{a}}$$ between $$t = 0$$ and $$t = x$$ where $$a &gt; 0$$ and $$a \neq 1$$ is fixed, and evaluate the limit as $$x\rightarrow\infty.$$</paragraph>
